#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:8
msgid "Setting up Turtlesim - how-to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:10
msgid ""
"Turtlesim is a simple simulator to demonstrate core ROS concepts without any "
"hardware. This article walks you through installation of Turtlesim and the "
"rqt GUI. A short exercise provides you with basic experience with these "
"tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:14
msgid "**Area: Framework | Content-type: how-to | Experience: beginner**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:18
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:21
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:23
msgid ""
"Turtlesim is a lightweight simulator for learning ROS basics. Install the "
"package ``ros-rolling-turtlesim``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:26
msgid ""
"The rqt tool is a graphical interface for interacting with ROS. Install the "
"package ``ros-rolling-rqt``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:30
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:32
msgid ""
"Before you start, make sure ROS is installed and your environment is "
"configured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:34
msgid ""
"To learn how to set up your environment, see :doc:`../Configuring-ROS2-"
"Environment`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:37
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:40
msgid ""
"Do not forget to source ROS in every new terminal you open. See :doc:"
"`Configuring environment <../Configuring-ROS2-Environment>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:44
msgid "1 Install Turtlesim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:46
msgid ""
"Turtlesim is a lightweight simulator that represents a robot as a turtle you "
"can control on the screen. It lets you practice core ROS concepts without "
"the need for any real hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:49
msgid "Install the Turtlesim package for your ROS distribution:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:53
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:100
msgid "Ubuntu"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:55
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt update\n"
"$ sudo apt install ros-rolling-turtlesim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:60
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:107
msgid "RHEL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:62
msgid "$ sudo dnf install ros-rolling-turtlesim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:66
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:113
msgid "macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:68
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:72
msgid ""
"As long as the archive you installed ROS from contains the ``ros_tutorials`` "
"repository, you should already have Turtlesim installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:70
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:117
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:74
msgid "To check if the package is installed, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:76
msgid "$ ros2 pkg executables turtlesim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:80
msgid "The output should list Turtlesim's executables:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:82
msgid ""
"turtlesim draw_square\n"
"turtlesim mimic\n"
"turtlesim turtle_teleop_key\n"
"turtlesim turtlesim_node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:90
msgid "2 Install rqt (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:92
msgid ""
"The rqt tool is a graphical interface for ROS. Instead of typing commands by "
"hand, you can use rqt to explore and call Turtlesim's services with a few "
"clicks. For more information about rqt, see :doc:`../../Developer-Tools/"
"Visualization/About-RQt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:96
msgid "In a new terminal, install ``rqt`` and the common plugins:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:102
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt update\n"
"$ sudo apt install ros-rolling-rqt ros-rolling-rqt-common-plugins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:109
msgid "$ sudo dnf install 'ros-rolling-rqt*'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:115
msgid ""
"The standard archive for installing ROS on macOS contains ``rqt`` and its "
"plugins, so you should already have ``rqt`` installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:119
msgid ""
"The standard archive for installing ROS on Windows contains ``rqt`` and its "
"plugins, so you should already have ``rqt`` installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:121
msgid "To check if the packages are installed, in a terminal, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:123
msgid "$ ros2 pkg list | grep -E '^rqt_gui$|^rqt_common_plugins$'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:127
msgid "The output should include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:129
msgid ""
"rqt_common_plugins\n"
"rqt_gui"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:136
msgid ""
"If the packages do not appear in the list, make sure you have sourced ROS in "
"the current terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:139
msgid "3 Try out Turtlesim with rqt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:141
msgid ""
"The following example uses rqt but you can also operate Turtlesim by "
"entering the same commands in the command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:143
msgid "Start Turtlesim:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:145
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run turtlesim turtlesim_node\n"
"[INFO] [turtlesim]: Starting turtlesim with node name /turtlesim\n"
"[INFO] [turtlesim]: Spawning turtle [turtle1] at x=[5.544445], y=[5.544445], "
"theta=[0.000000]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:151
msgid "The simulator window opens with a random turtle in the center."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:155
msgid "In a new terminal, source ROS again and start keyboard teleoperation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:157
msgid "$ ros2 run turtlesim turtle_teleop_key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:161
msgid ""
"Keep the ``turtle_teleop_key`` terminal active and use arrow keys to move "
"the turtle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:165
msgid ""
"Pressing an arrow key causes the turtle to move a short distance and then "
"stop. This behaviour ensures a robot doesn't continue carrying on an "
"instruction if, for example, the operator loses connection to the robot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:168
msgid ""
"(Optional) List the active nodes, topics, services, and actions. This will "
"help you verify what is currently running and available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:171
msgid "In a new terminal, source ROS again, then run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:173
msgid ""
"$ ros2 node list\n"
"$ ros2 topic list\n"
"$ ros2 service list\n"
"$ ros2 action list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:180
msgid ""
"``ros2 node list`` shows the nodes currently running in the system. ``ros2 "
"topic list`` shows the topics through which nodes exchange data. ``ros2 "
"service list`` shows the services nodes expose for request-response "
"interactions. ``ros2 action list`` shows the actions available for long-"
"running tasks such as rotating the turtle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:185
msgid "Start rqt:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:187
msgid "$ rqt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:191
msgid "In rqt, select **Plugins** > **Services** > **Service Caller**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:195
msgid ""
"It may take some time for rqt to locate all the plugins. If you click on "
"**Plugins** but don't see **Services** or any other options, close rqt and "
"enter the command ``rqt --force-discover`` in your terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:200
msgid ""
"You might need to select the **Refresh Service** button to the left of the "
"**Service** drop-down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:204
msgid "To spawn a second turtle, select the ``/spawn`` service, then enter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:206
msgid "``name`` = ``turtle2``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:207
msgid "``x`` = ``1.0``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:208
msgid "``y`` = ``1.0``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:210
msgid "Click **Call**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:216
msgid ""
"Each turtle needs a unique name. If you spawn a turtle with an existing "
"name, you get an error message in the terminal that runs ``turtlesim_node``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:219
msgid "[ERROR] [turtlesim]: A turtle named [turtle1] already exists"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:223
msgid ""
"Set the turtle to draw a red, thicker line. Select the ``/turtle1/set_pen`` "
"service, then set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:226
msgid "``r`` = ``255``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:227
msgid "``width`` = ``5``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:229
msgid ""
"Click **Call**, then use arrow keys in the teleoperation terminal to confirm "
"the turtle draws a red, thicker line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:235
msgid "Set up a teleoperation node for ``turtle2``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:237
msgid ""
"By default, ``turtle_teleop_key`` sends commands to topics and actions under "
"the ``turtle1`` namespace. To control ``turtle2`` instead, use the ``--"
"remap`` option to point those topics and actions at the ``turtle2`` "
"namespace. This lets you reuse the same executable for a different turtle "
"without changing any code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:241
msgid "In a new terminal, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:243
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run turtlesim turtle_teleop_key --ros-args --remap turtle1/cmd_vel:"
"=turtle2/cmd_vel --remap turtle1/rotate_absolute:=turtle2/rotate_absolute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:247
msgid ""
"Keep this new terminal active to move ``turtle2``. Continue using the "
"original teleoperation terminal to move ``turtle1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:252
msgid "Close Turtlesim:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:254
msgid "In the ``turtlesim_node`` terminal, press ``Ctrl + C``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:255
msgid "In ``turtle_teleop_key`` terminals, press ``q``."
msgstr ""

