#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:274
msgid "FAQs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:276
msgid "Do I need rqt to use Turtlesim?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:277
msgid ""
"No. You can use Turtlesim entirely from the command line. The rqt tool is "
"recommended because it helps you visualize the instructions you send to the "
"turtle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:281
msgid "Why can I move only one turtle at a time?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:282
msgid ""
"Each ``turtle_teleop_key`` instance controls one turtle namespace. To "
"control ``turtle2``, run a second teleop node with topic and action "
"remapping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:285
msgid "Why doesn't the turtle move when I press the arrow keys?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim.rst:286
msgid ""
"The ``turtle_teleop_key`` terminal must be the active window for it to "
"capture your key presses. Each press also moves the turtle only a short "
"distance, so you need to press the keys repeatedly to keep the turtle moving."
msgstr ""
